{"format":1,"name":"Orchestron 90","assembly":"// ===========================================================================\n//  ORCHESTRON 90 — a 90s-style string ensemble synth\n//  8 voices, 3 detuned saws + sub square per voice, 2-pole SVF with envelope\n//  modulation, a 3-tap ensemble chorus and a Schroeder plate reverb.\n// ===========================================================================\n\nconst MAX_FRAMES: i32 = 8192;\nconst MAX_CHANNELS: i32 = 2;\nconst MAX_PARAMS: i32 = 64;\n\nconst NV: i32 = 8;              // polyphony\nconst CH_LEN: i32 = 4096;       // ensemble delay line\nconst CH_MASK: i32 = CH_LEN - 1;\nconst NLINES: i32 = 12;         // reverb delay lines\nconst REV_LEN: i32 = 14000;\n\nconst inBuf  = new StaticArray<f32>(MAX_FRAMES * MAX_CHANNELS);\nconst outBuf = new StaticArray<f32>(MAX_FRAMES * MAX_CHANNELS);\nconst params = new StaticArray<f32>(MAX_PARAMS);\n\nlet sampleRate: f32 = 44100;\nlet channels: i32 = 2;\n\n// ---- voice state ----------------------------------------------------------\nconst vP1 = new StaticArray<f32>(NV);\nconst vP2 = new StaticArray<f32>(NV);\nconst vP3 = new StaticArray<f32>(NV);\nconst vPS = new StaticArray<f32>(NV);   // sub phase\nconst vFreq = new StaticArray<f32>(NV);\nconst vVel = new StaticArray<f32>(NV);\nconst vEnv = new StaticArray<f32>(NV);\nconst vStage = new StaticArray<i32>(NV); // 0 idle 1 atk 2 dec 3 sus 4 rel\nconst vNote = new StaticArray<i32>(NV);\nconst vAge = new StaticArray<i32>(NV);\nconst vI1 = new StaticArray<f32>(NV);   // svf state\nconst vI2 = new StaticArray<f32>(NV);\nlet ageCounter: i32 = 1;\n\n// ---- ensemble chorus -----------------------------------------------------\nconst chBuf = new StaticArray<f32>(CH_LEN);\nlet chIdx: i32 = 0;\nlet lfoPh: f32 = 0;\n\n// ---- reverb --------------------------------------------------------------\nconst revBuf = new StaticArray<f32>(REV_LEN);\nconst lineOff = new StaticArray<i32>(NLINES);\nconst lineLen = new StaticArray<i32>(NLINES);\nconst lineIdx = new StaticArray<i32>(NLINES);\nconst combF = new StaticArray<f32>(NLINES);\n\nfunction clampf(x: f32, lo: f32, hi: f32): f32 {\n  if (x < lo) return lo;\n  if (x > hi) return hi;\n  return x;\n}\n\nexport function init(sr: f32, maxFrames: i32, ch: i32): void {\n  sampleRate = sr > 8000 ? sr : 44100;\n  channels = ch < MAX_CHANNELS ? ch : MAX_CHANNELS;\n\n  for (let v = 0; v < NV; v++) {\n    vP1[v] = f32(v) * 0.11;\n    vP2[v] = f32(v) * 0.27;\n    vP3[v] = f32(v) * 0.53;\n    vPS[v] = 0;\n    vFreq[v] = 220;\n    vVel[v] = 0;\n    vEnv[v] = 0;\n    vStage[v] = 0;\n    vNote[v] = -1;\n    vAge[v] = 0;\n    vI1[v] = 0;\n    vI2[v] = 0;\n  }\n\n  for (let i = 0; i < CH_LEN; i++) chBuf[i] = 0;\n  chIdx = 0;\n  lfoPh = 0;\n\n  // reverb line lengths (freeverb-ish), stereo spread of 23 samples\n  const baseLen = [1116, 1188, 1277, 1356, 556, 441];\n  let scale: f32 = sampleRate / 44100.0;\n  if (scale > 1.15) scale = 1.15;\n  if (scale < 0.5) scale = 0.5;\n  let off: i32 = 0;\n  for (let k = 0; k < NLINES; k++) {\n    const half: i32 = k < 6 ? k : k - 6;\n    let len: i32 = i32(f32(baseLen[half]) * scale) + (k < 6 ? 0 : 23);\n    if (len < 8) len = 8;\n    lineLen[k] = len;\n    lineOff[k] = off;\n    lineIdx[k] = 0;\n    combF[k] = 0;\n    off += len;\n  }\n  for (let i = 0; i < REV_LEN; i++) revBuf[i] = 0;\n\n  // defaults\n  params[0] = 0.45;    // attack\n  params[1] = 0.40;    // decay\n  params[2] = 0.85;    // sustain\n  params[3] = 0.55;    // release\n  params[4] = 3200.0;  // cutoff Hz\n  params[5] = 0.18;    // resonance\n  params[6] = 0.35;    // env -> cutoff\n  params[7] = 0.40;    // detune\n  params[8] = 0.60;    // ensemble rate Hz\n  params[9] = 0.65;    // ensemble depth\n  params[10] = 0.70;   // ensemble mix\n  params[11] = 0.30;   // sub level\n  params[12] = 0.35;   // reverb mix\n  params[13] = 0.60;   // reverb size\n  params[14] = 0.70;   // output level\n}\n\nexport function getInputPtr(): usize  { return changetype<usize>(inBuf); }\nexport function getOutputPtr(): usize { return changetype<usize>(outBuf); }\nexport function getParamsPtr(): usize { return changetype<usize>(params); }\nexport function getNumParams(): i32   { return 15; }\n\nexport function noteOn(id: i32, f: f32, v: f32): void {\n  // reuse a voice already holding this note, else a free one, else steal oldest\n  let slot: i32 = -1;\n  for (let i = 0; i < NV; i++) {\n    if (vNote[i] == id && vStage[i] != 0) { slot = i; break; }\n  }\n  if (slot < 0) {\n    for (let i = 0; i < NV; i++) {\n      if (vStage[i] == 0) { slot = i; break; }\n    }\n  }\n  if (slot < 0) {\n    let oldest: i32 = 0x7fffffff;\n    for (let i = 0; i < NV; i++) {\n      if (vAge[i] < oldest) { oldest = vAge[i]; slot = i; }\n    }\n  }\n  vNote[slot] = id;\n  vFreq[slot] = f > 8.0 ? f : 8.0;\n  vVel[slot] = clampf(v > 1.0 ? v / 127.0 : v, 0.05, 1.0);\n  vStage[slot] = 1;\n  vAge[slot] = ageCounter++;\n}\n\nexport function noteOff(id: i32): void {\n  for (let i = 0; i < NV; i++) {\n    if (vNote[i] == id && vStage[i] != 0 && vStage[i] != 4) vStage[i] = 4;\n  }\n}\n\nfunction combProc(k: i32, x: f32, fb: f32, damp: f32): f32 {\n  const off: i32 = lineOff[k];\n  const len: i32 = lineLen[k];\n  let idx: i32 = lineIdx[k];\n  const y: f32 = revBuf[off + idx];\n  let fl: f32 = combF[k];\n  fl = f32(y * (1.0 - damp) + fl * damp);\n  combF[k] = fl;\n  revBuf[off + idx] = f32(x + fl * fb);\n  idx++;\n  if (idx >= len) idx = 0;\n  lineIdx[k] = idx;\n  return y;\n}\n\nfunction apProc(k: i32, x: f32): f32 {\n  const off: i32 = lineOff[k];\n  const len: i32 = lineLen[k];\n  let idx: i32 = lineIdx[k];\n  const y: f32 = revBuf[off + idx];\n  revBuf[off + idx] = f32(x + y * 0.5);\n  idx++;\n  if (idx >= len) idx = 0;\n  lineIdx[k] = idx;\n  return f32(y - x);\n}\n\nfunction readCh(delaySamples: f32): f32 {\n  let pos: f32 = f32(chIdx) - delaySamples;\n  while (pos < 0) pos += f32(CH_LEN);\n  const i0: i32 = i32(pos) & CH_MASK;\n  const i1: i32 = (i0 + 1) & CH_MASK;\n  const frac: f32 = pos - Mathf.floor(pos);\n  const a: f32 = chBuf[i0];\n  const b: f32 = chBuf[i1];\n  return f32(a + (b - a) * frac);\n}\n\nfunction softClip(x: f32): f32 {\n  if (x > 1.6) return 1.0;\n  if (x < -1.6) return -1.0;\n  return f32(x - (x * x * x) * 0.14);\n}\n\nexport function process(n: i32): void {\n  const sr: f32 = sampleRate;\n\n  // --- envelope rates ---\n  const atkT: f32 = f32(0.004 + clampf(params[0], 0, 1) * clampf(params[0], 0, 1) * 3.0);\n  const decT: f32 = f32(0.03 + clampf(params[1], 0, 1) * clampf(params[1], 0, 1) * 3.0);\n  const sus: f32 = clampf(params[2], 0, 1);\n  const relT: f32 = f32(0.03 + clampf(params[3], 0, 1) * clampf(params[3], 0, 1) * 4.5);\n  const aInc: f32 = f32(1.0 / (atkT * sr));\n  const dInc: f32 = f32((1.0 - sus) / (decT * sr) + 0.0000001);\n  const rInc: f32 = f32(1.0 / (relT * sr));\n\n  // --- tone ---\n  const cutoff: f32 = clampf(params[4], 40.0, 16000.0);\n  const reso: f32 = clampf(params[5], 0, 1);\n  const envMod: f32 = clampf(params[6], 0, 1);\n  const detune: f32 = clampf(params[7], 0, 1) * 0.022;\n  const subAmt: f32 = clampf(params[11], 0, 1) * 0.7;\n  const kDamp: f32 = f32(2.0 - 1.85 * reso);\n\n  // --- ensemble ---\n  const rate: f32 = clampf(params[8], 0.02, 8.0);\n  const depth: f32 = clampf(params[9], 0, 1);\n  const ensMix: f32 = clampf(params[10], 0, 1);\n  const lfoInc: f32 = f32(rate / sr);\n  const baseD: f32 = f32(0.010 * sr);\n  const modD: f32 = f32(0.0055 * sr * depth);\n\n  // --- reverb ---\n  const revMix: f32 = clampf(params[12], 0, 1);\n  const size: f32 = clampf(params[13], 0, 1);\n  const fb: f32 = f32(0.70 + size * 0.27);\n  const damp: f32 = f32(0.18 + (1.0 - size) * 0.30);\n\n  const level: f32 = clampf(params[14], 0, 1);\n  const TWO_PI: f32 = 6.2831855;\n\n  for (let f = 0; f < n; f++) {\n    let mono: f32 = 0;\n\n    for (let v = 0; v < NV; v++) {\n      const stage: i32 = vStage[v];\n      if (stage == 0) continue;\n\n      // envelope\n      let e: f32 = vEnv[v];\n      if (stage == 1) {\n        e += aInc;\n        if (e >= 1.0) { e = 1.0; vStage[v] = 2; }\n      } else if (stage == 2) {\n        e -= dInc;\n        if (e <= sus) { e = sus; vStage[v] = 3; }\n      } else if (stage == 3) {\n        e = sus;\n        if (sus <= 0.0001) { e = 0; vStage[v] = 0; vNote[v] = -1; }\n      } else {\n        e -= rInc;\n        if (e <= 0.0) { e = 0; vStage[v] = 0; vNote[v] = -1; }\n      }\n      vEnv[v] = e;\n      if (vStage[v] == 0) continue;\n\n      // three detuned saws + sub square\n      const fr: f32 = vFreq[v];\n      const i1: f32 = f32(fr / sr);\n      const i2: f32 = f32(fr * (1.0 + detune) / sr);\n      const i3: f32 = f32(fr * (1.0 - detune * 0.85) / sr);\n      const iS: f32 = f32(fr * 0.5 / sr);\n\n      let p1: f32 = vP1[v] + i1; if (p1 >= 1.0) p1 -= 1.0;\n      let p2: f32 = vP2[v] + i2; if (p2 >= 1.0) p2 -= 1.0;\n      let p3: f32 = vP3[v] + i3; if (p3 >= 1.0) p3 -= 1.0;\n      let ps: f32 = vPS[v] + iS; if (ps >= 1.0) ps -= 1.0;\n      vP1[v] = p1; vP2[v] = p2; vP3[v] = p3; vPS[v] = ps;\n\n      let x: f32 = f32((p1 * 2.0 - 1.0) + (p2 * 2.0 - 1.0) + (p3 * 2.0 - 1.0)) * 0.30;\n      x += (ps < 0.5 ? f32(1.0) : f32(-1.0)) * subAmt * 0.30;\n\n      // 2-pole SVF, cutoff tracked by envelope\n      let fc: f32 = f32(cutoff * (1.0 + envMod * 5.0 * e));\n      const nyq: f32 = f32(sr * 0.45);\n      if (fc > nyq) fc = nyq;\n      if (fc < 30.0) fc = 30.0;\n      const g: f32 = Mathf.tan(f32(3.14159265 * fc / sr));\n      const a1: f32 = f32(1.0 / (1.0 + g * (g + kDamp)));\n      const a2: f32 = f32(g * a1);\n      const a3: f32 = f32(g * a2);\n      let ic1: f32 = vI1[v];\n      let ic2: f32 = vI2[v];\n      const v3: f32 = f32(x - ic2);\n      const vv1: f32 = f32(a1 * ic1 + a2 * v3);\n      const vv2: f32 = f32(ic2 + a2 * ic1 + a3 * v3);\n      ic1 = f32(2.0 * vv1 - ic1);\n      ic2 = f32(2.0 * vv2 - ic2);\n      vI1[v] = ic1;\n      vI2[v] = ic2;\n\n      mono += f32(vv2 * e * vVel[v]);\n    }\n\n    mono *= 0.42;\n\n    // ---- ensemble chorus (3 modulated taps, spread across the stereo field)\n    chBuf[chIdx] = mono;\n    lfoPh += lfoInc;\n    if (lfoPh >= 1.0) lfoPh -= 1.0;\n    const m1: f32 = Mathf.sin(f32(TWO_PI * lfoPh));\n    const m2: f32 = Mathf.sin(f32(TWO_PI * (lfoPh + 0.3333)));\n    const m3: f32 = Mathf.sin(f32(TWO_PI * (lfoPh + 0.6667)));\n    const t1: f32 = readCh(f32(baseD + modD * (1.0 + m1)));\n    const t2: f32 = readCh(f32(baseD * 1.35 + modD * (1.0 + m2)));\n    const t3: f32 = readCh(f32(baseD * 1.75 + modD * (1.0 + m3)));\n    chIdx = (chIdx + 1) & CH_MASK;\n\n    const wetL: f32 = f32(t1 * 0.62 + t3 * 0.38);\n    const wetR: f32 = f32(t2 * 0.62 + t3 * 0.38);\n    let dl: f32 = f32(mono * (1.0 - ensMix * 0.45) + wetL * ensMix);\n    let dr: f32 = f32(mono * (1.0 - ensMix * 0.45) + wetR * ensMix);\n\n    // ---- plate reverb ----\n    if (revMix > 0.001) {\n      const rin: f32 = f32((dl + dr) * 0.5 * 0.30);\n      let sL: f32 = 0;\n      sL += combProc(0, rin, fb, damp);\n      sL += combProc(1, rin, fb, damp);\n      sL += combProc(2, rin, fb, damp);\n      sL += combProc(3, rin, fb, damp);\n      sL *= 0.25;\n      sL = apProc(4, sL);\n      sL = apProc(5, sL);\n      let sR: f32 = 0;\n      sR += combProc(6, rin, fb, damp);\n      sR += combProc(7, rin, fb, damp);\n      sR += combProc(8, rin, fb, damp);\n      sR += combProc(9, rin, fb, damp);\n      sR *= 0.25;\n      sR = apProc(10, sR);\n      sR = apProc(11, sR);\n      dl = f32(dl * (1.0 - revMix * 0.5) + sL * revMix * 1.6);\n      dr = f32(dr * (1.0 - revMix * 0.5) + sR * revMix * 1.6);\n    }\n\n    const oL: f32 = softClip(f32(dl * level * 1.5));\n    const oR: f32 = softClip(f32(dr * level * 1.5));\n    outBuf[f] = oL;\n    outBuf[MAX_FRAMES + f] = oR;\n  }\n}\n","html":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\"/>\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"/>\n<title>Orchestron 90</title>\n<style>\n  :root{\n    --bg:#171717;\n    --panel:#1f1f1f;\n    --panel-2:#262626;\n    --track:#0d0d0d;\n    --line:rgba(255,255,255,.06);\n    --line-2:rgba(255,255,255,.11);\n    --line-3:rgba(255,255,255,.20);\n    --edge:rgba(255,255,255,.05);\n    --ink:#d7d7d9;\n    --ink-2:#9a9b9e;\n    --muted:#67696e;\n    --accent:#c8923a;\n    --accent-2:#3fa98c;\n    --radius:3px;\n    --radius-sm:2px;\n  }\n\n  *{box-sizing:border-box}\n  html,body{margin:0;height:100%}\n  body{\n    background:var(--bg);\n    color:var(--ink);\n    font:11px/1.4 ui-sans-serif,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,\"Segoe UI\",system-ui,sans-serif;\n    -webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;\n    -webkit-user-select:none;\n    user-select:none;\n    overflow-y:auto;\n  }\n\n  .app{display:flex;flex-direction:column;min-height:100%}\n\n  /* ---- top bar ---- */\n  .topbar{\n    display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:10px;\n    height:34px;padding:0 12px;\n    background:var(--panel);\n    border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);\n  }\n  .topbar .brand{font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink)}\n  .topbar .tagline{font-size:9px;letter-spacing:1.2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted)}\n  .topbar .sp{flex:1}\n  .topbar .hint{font-size:9px;letter-spacing:.6px;color:var(--muted)}\n  .topbar .hint b{color:var(--accent);font-weight:600}\n\n  .page{padding:10px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px}\n  .row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px;align-items:stretch}\n\n  /* ---- panels ---- */\n  .panel{\n    background:var(--panel);\n    border:1px solid var(--line);\n    border-top-color:var(--edge);\n    border-radius:var(--radius);\n    min-width:0;\n  }\n  .panel>.head{\n    display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;height:22px;padding:0 9px;\n    font-size:9px;letter-spacing:1.2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted);\n    border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);\n  }\n  .panel>.head .dot{width:5px;height:5px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--accent);opacity:.75}\n  .panel>.body{padding:10px;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start}\n\n  /* ---- control cell ---- */\n  .cell{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:4px;min-width:0}\n  .cell .lbl{font-size:9px;letter-spacing:.7px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-2);white-space:nowrap}\n  .num{\n    font-size:10px;color:var(--ink);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;\n    background:var(--track);border:1px solid var(--line-2);border-radius:var(--radius-sm);\n    padding:1px 6px;min-width:56px;text-align:center;\n  }\n\n  /* ---- knob ---- */\n  .knob{cursor:ns-resize;touch-action:none;display:block}\n  .knob .face{fill:var(--track);stroke:var(--line-2);stroke-width:1}\n  .knob .track{fill:none;stroke:var(--line-2);stroke-width:2.5}\n  .knob .arc{fill:none;stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:2.5;stroke-linecap:butt}\n  .knob .ind{stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:2;stroke-linecap:round}\n\n  /* ---- displays ---- */\n  .disp{position:relative;background:var(--track);border:1px solid var(--line-2);border-radius:var(--radius-sm)}\n  .disp canvas{display:block;width:100%;height:100%}\n  .disp .tag{position:absolute;top:4px;left:6px;font-size:8px;letter-spacing:.9px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted)}\n  .disp .rd{position:absolute;top:4px;right:6px;font-size:9px;color:var(--ink-2);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}\n\n  /* ---- buttons ---- */\n  .btn{\n    appearance:none;border:1px solid var(--line-2);border-top-color:var(--edge);\n    background:var(--panel-2);color:var(--ink-2);font:inherit;font-size:10px;font-weight:600;\n    letter-spacing:.4px;padding:4px 9px;border-radius:var(--radius-sm);cursor:pointer;min-width:30px;\n  }\n  .btn:hover{border-color:var(--line-3);color:var(--ink)}\n  .btn:active{background:var(--panel)}\n\n  /* ---- piano ---- */\n  .kbwrap{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;width:100%}\n  .kbbar{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px}\n  .kbbar .oct{font-size:9px;letter-spacing:.8px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-2);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}\n  .piano{\n    position:relative;height:80px;display:flex;\n    border:1px solid var(--line-2);border-radius:var(--radius-sm);\n    overflow:hidden;background:#000;touch-action:none;\n  }\n  .wk{\n    flex:1;background:#cbccce;border-right:1px solid #232323;cursor:pointer;\n    display:flex;align-items:flex-end;justify-content:center;padding-bottom:4px;\n  }\n  .wk.down{background:var(--accent)}\n  .bk{\n    position:absolute;top:0;width:5%;height:62%;background:#1c1c1e;z-index:2;cursor:pointer;\n    border:1px solid #000;border-top:0;border-radius:0 0 2px 2px;\n    display:flex;align-items:flex-end;justify-content:center;padding-bottom:3px;\n  }\n  .bk.down{background:var(--accent)}\n  .kl{font-size:8px;letter-spacing:.4px;color:#5a5b5e;pointer-events:none}\n  .bk .kl{color:#8c8d90}\n  .wk.down .kl,.bk.down .kl{color:#1a1206}\n\n  .tip{\n    position:fixed;z-index:50;background:#000;color:var(--ink);\n    border:1px solid var(--line-2);border-radius:var(--radius-sm);\n    padding:3px 7px;font-size:10px;pointer-events:none;white-space:nowrap;\n    opacity:0;transition:opacity .08s;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;\n  }\n  .tip.show{opacity:1}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"app\">\n\n  <div class=\"topbar\">\n    <span class=\"brand\">Orchestron 90</span>\n    <span class=\"tagline\">String Ensemble</span>\n    <span class=\"sp\"></span>\n    <span class=\"hint\">play with <b>A</b>&hairsp;…&hairsp;<b>;</b></span>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"page\">\n\n    <div class=\"row\">\n\n      <div class=\"panel\" style=\"flex:1 1 340px\">\n        <div class=\"head\"><span class=\"dot\"></span>Contour</div>\n        <div class=\"body\">\n          <div class=\"disp adsr\" style=\"flex:1 1 170px;height:118px;min-width:150px\">\n            <span class=\"tag\">Envelope</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"cell\">\n            <div class=\"knob-host\" data-index=\"0\" data-min=\"0\" data-max=\"1\" data-def=\"0.45\" data-disp=\"atk\"></div>\n            <div class=\"lbl\">Attack</div><div class=\"num\"></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"cell\">\n            <div class=\"knob-host\" data-index=\"1\" data-min=\"0\" data-max=\"1\" data-def=\"0.40\" data-disp=\"dec\"></div>\n            <div class=\"lbl\">Decay</div><div class=\"num\"></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"cell\">\n            <div class=\"knob-host\" data-index=\"2\" data-min=\"0\" data-max=\"1\" data-def=\"0.85\" data-disp=\"pct\"></div>\n            <div class=\"lbl\">Sustain</div><div class=\"num\"></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"cell\">\n            <div class=\"knob-host\" data-index=\"3\" data-min=\"0\" data-max=\"1\" data-def=\"0.55\" data-disp=\"rel\"></div>\n            <div class=\"lbl\">Release</div><div class=\"num\"></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"panel\" style=\"flex:1 1 300px\">\n        <div class=\"head\"><span class=\"dot\"></span>Tone</div>\n        <div class=\"body\">\n          <div class=\"cell\">\n            <div class=\"knob-host\" data-index=\"4\" data-min=\"60\" data-max=\"14000\" data-def=\"3200\" data-log=\"1\" data-disp=\"hz\"></div>\n            <div class=\"lbl\">Cutoff</div><div class=\"num\"></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"cell\">\n            <div class=\"knob-host\" data-index=\"5\" data-min=\"0\" data-max=\"1\" data-def=\"0.18\" data-disp=\"pct\"></div>\n            <div class=\"lbl\">Reso</div><div class=\"num\"></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"cell\">\n            <div class=\"knob-host\" data-index=\"6\" data-min=\"0\" data-max=\"1\" data-def=\"0.35\" data-disp=\"pct\"></div>\n            <div class=\"lbl\">Env&nbsp;Amt</div><div class=\"num\"></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"cell\">\n            <div class=\"knob-host\" data-index=\"7\" data-min=\"0\" data-max=\"1\" data-def=\"0.40\" data-disp=\"pct\"></div>\n            <div class=\"lbl\">Detune</div><div class=\"num\"></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"cell\">\n            <div class=\"knob-host\" data-index=\"11\" data-min=\"0\" data-max=\"1\" data-def=\"0.30\" data-disp=\"pct\"></div>\n            <div class=\"lbl\">Sub</div><div class=\"num\"></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"row\">\n\n      <div class=\"panel\" style=\"flex:1 1 340px\">\n        <div class=\"head\"><span class=\"dot\"></span>Ensemble</div>\n        <div class=\"body\">\n          <div class=\"disp ens\" style=\"flex:1 1 160px;height:96px;min-width:140px\">\n            <span class=\"tag\">Chorus</span><span class=\"rd\"></span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"cell\">\n            <div class=\"knob-host\" data-index=\"8\" data-min=\"0.05\" data-max=\"8\" data-def=\"0.60\" data-log=\"1\" data-disp=\"rate\"></div>\n            <div class=\"lbl\">Rate</div><div class=\"num\"></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"cell\">\n            <div class=\"knob-host\" data-index=\"9\" data-min=\"0\" data-max=\"1\" data-def=\"0.65\" data-disp=\"pct\"></div>\n            <div class=\"lbl\">Depth</div><div class=\"num\"></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"cell\">\n            <div class=\"knob-host\" data-index=\"10\" data-min=\"0\" data-max=\"1\" data-def=\"0.70\" data-disp=\"pct\"></div>\n            <div class=\"lbl\">Mix</div><div class=\"num\"></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"panel\" style=\"flex:1 1 230px\">\n        <div class=\"head\"><span class=\"dot\"></span>Space / Output</div>\n        <div class=\"body\">\n          <div class=\"cell\">\n            <div class=\"knob-host\" data-index=\"12\" data-min=\"0\" data-max=\"1\" data-def=\"0.35\" data-disp=\"pct\"></div>\n            <div class=\"lbl\">Reverb</div><div class=\"num\"></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"cell\">\n            <div class=\"knob-host\" data-index=\"13\" data-min=\"0\" data-max=\"1\" data-def=\"0.60\" data-disp=\"pct\"></div>\n            <div class=\"lbl\">Size</div><div class=\"num\"></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"cell\">\n            <div class=\"knob-host\" data-index=\"14\" data-min=\"0\" data-max=\"1\" data-def=\"0.70\" data-disp=\"pct\" data-size=\"62\"></div>\n            <div class=\"lbl\">Level</div><div class=\"num\"></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"panel\">\n      <div class=\"head\"><span class=\"dot\"></span>Keyboard</div>\n      <div class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"kbwrap\">\n          <div class=\"kbbar\">\n            <button class=\"btn\" id=\"octDown\">Oct &minus;</button>\n            <span class=\"oct\" id=\"octLabel\">C4</span>\n            <button class=\"btn\" id=\"octUp\">Oct +</button>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"piano\" id=\"kbd\"></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<script>\n\"use strict\";\n\n/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *\n * Engine bridge\n * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */\nfunction whenReady(cb){\n  function go(){ (window.vstai.onReady ? window.vstai.onReady(cb) : cb()); }\n  if (window.vstai) return go();\n  const t = setInterval(() => {\n    if (window.vstai) { clearInterval(t); go(); }\n  }, 25);\n}\n\nconst PV = {};   // last known value of every param, for the visualisers\n\nfunction setParam(i, v){\n  PV[i] = v;\n  if (window.vstai) window.vstai.setParam(i, v);\n}\n\nfunction onParam(cb){\n  if (window.vstai && window.vstai.onParam) window.vstai.onParam(cb);\n}\n\nfunction noteOnHost(n, v){\n  if (window.vstai && window.vstai.noteOn) window.vstai.noteOn(n, v);\n}\n\nfunction noteOffHost(n){\n  if (window.vstai && window.vstai.noteOff) window.vstai.noteOff(n);\n}\n\nconst clamp = (v, a, b) => Math.max(a, Math.min(b, v));\nconst ns = \"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\";\n\nfunction svgEl(t, a){\n  const e = document.createElementNS(ns, t);\n  for (const k in a) e.setAttribute(k, a[k]);\n  return e;\n}\n\n/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *\n * Tooltip\n * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */\nconst tip = document.createElement(\"div\");\ntip.className = \"tip\";\ndocument.body.append(tip);\n\nfunction showTip(text, x, y){\n  tip.textContent = text;\n  tip.style.left = (x + 12) + \"px\";\n  tip.style.top = (y + 14) + \"px\";\n  tip.classList.add(\"show\");\n}\n\nfunction hideTip(){\n  tip.classList.remove(\"show\");\n}\n\n/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *\n * Value formatting — mirrors the DSP's own param mappings\n * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */\nconst attackSec  = p => 0.004 + p * p * 3.0;\nconst decaySec   = p => 0.03 + p * p * 3.0;\nconst releaseSec = p => 0.03 + p * p * 4.5;\n\nfunction fmtTime(s){\n  return s < 1 ? Math.round(s * 1000) + \" ms\" : s.toFixed(2) + \" s\";\n}\n\nfunction formatValue(mode, v){\n  switch (mode){\n    case \"pct\":  return Math.round(v * 100) + \" %\";\n    case \"hz\":   return v >= 1000 ? (v / 1000).toFixed(2) + \" kHz\" : Math.round(v) + \" Hz\";\n    case \"rate\": return v.toFixed(2) + \" Hz\";\n    case \"atk\":  return fmtTime(attackSec(v));\n    case \"dec\":  return fmtTime(decaySec(v));\n    case \"rel\":  return fmtTime(releaseSec(v));\n    default:     return v.toFixed(2);\n  }\n}\n\n/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *\n * Knob — flat recessed disc, thin value arc, single indicator line\n * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */\nfunction makeKnob(host){\n  const i = +host.dataset.index;\n  const min = +host.dataset.min;\n  const max = +host.dataset.max;\n  const def = +host.dataset.def;\n  const log = host.dataset.log === \"1\";\n  const mode = host.dataset.disp || \"num\";\n  const size = host.dataset.size ? +host.dataset.size : 54;\n  const num = host.parentElement.querySelector(\".num\");\n\n  host.style.width = host.style.height = size + \"px\";\n\n  const svg = svgEl(\"svg\", { class: \"knob\", viewBox: \"0 0 100 100\", width: size, height: size });\n  const a0 = 135, a1 = 405, R = 38;\n\n  const polar = (deg, r) => [50 + r * Math.cos(deg * Math.PI / 180), 50 + r * Math.sin(deg * Math.PI / 180)];\n\n  function arcPath(from, to, r){\n    const [sx, sy] = polar(from, r);\n    const [ex, ey] = polar(to, r);\n    return \"M \" + sx + \" \" + sy + \" A \" + r + \" \" + r + \" 0 \" + (to - from > 180 ? 1 : 0) + \" 1 \" + ex + \" \" + ey;\n  }\n\n  svg.append(svgEl(\"circle\", { class: \"face\", cx: 50, cy: 50, r: R - 6 }));\n  svg.append(svgEl(\"path\", { class: \"track\", d: arcPath(a0, a1, R) }));\n  const arc = svgEl(\"path\", { class: \"arc\" });\n  const ind = svgEl(\"line\", { class: \"ind\" });\n  svg.append(arc, ind);\n  host.append(svg);\n\n  const toNorm = v => log ? Math.log(v / min) / Math.log(max / min) : (v - min) / (max - min);\n  const fromNorm = n => log ? min * Math.pow(max / min, n) : min + n * (max - min);\n\n  let value = def;\n\n  function render(){\n    const n = clamp(toNorm(value), 0, 1);\n    const ang = a0 + n * (a1 - a0);\n    arc.setAttribute(\"d\", arcPath(a0, Math.max(a0 + 0.001, ang), R));\n    const [ix, iy] = polar(ang, 13);\n    const [ox, oy] = polar(ang, R - 2);\n    ind.setAttribute(\"x1\", ix); ind.setAttribute(\"y1\", iy);\n    ind.setAttribute(\"x2\", ox); ind.setAttribute(\"y2\", oy);\n    if (num) num.textContent = formatValue(mode, value);\n  }\n\n  function set(v){\n    value = clamp(v, min, max);\n    render();\n    setParam(i, value);\n  }\n\n  let drag = null;\n\n  svg.addEventListener(\"pointerdown\", e => {\n    if (e.button !== 0) return;\n    drag = { y: e.clientY, n: clamp(toNorm(value), 0, 1) };\n    svg.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId);\n    showTip(formatValue(mode, value), e.clientX, e.clientY);\n  });\n\n  svg.addEventListener(\"pointermove\", e => {\n    if (!drag) return;\n    const speed = e.shiftKey ? 900 : 210;\n    set(fromNorm(clamp(drag.n + (drag.y - e.clientY) / speed, 0, 1)));\n    showTip(formatValue(mode, value), e.clientX, e.clientY);\n  });\n\n  function endDrag(){\n    if (drag){ drag = null; hideTip(); }\n  }\n\n  svg.addEventListener(\"pointerup\", endDrag);\n  svg.addEventListener(\"pointercancel\", endDrag);\n\n  svg.addEventListener(\"wheel\", e => {\n    e.preventDefault();\n    const step = e.shiftKey ? 0.005 : 0.025;\n    set(fromNorm(clamp(toNorm(value) - Math.sign(e.deltaY) * step, 0, 1)));\n  }, { passive: false });\n\n  svg.addEventListener(\"dblclick\", () => set(def));\n\n  onParam((p, v) => {\n    if (p === i){\n      value = clamp(+v, min, max);\n      PV[i] = value;\n      render();\n    }\n  });\n\n  set(def);\n}\n\n/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *\n * Canvas helpers\n * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */\nfunction dispCanvas(host){\n  const c = document.createElement(\"canvas\");\n  host.append(c);\n  const ctx = c.getContext(\"2d\");\n\n  function fit(){\n    const dpr = window.devicePixelRatio || 1;\n    c.width = Math.max(1, Math.round(host.clientWidth * dpr));\n    c.height = Math.max(1, Math.round(host.clientHeight * dpr));\n    ctx.setTransform(dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0);\n    c._w = host.clientWidth;\n    c._h = host.clientHeight;\n  }\n\n  fit();\n  new ResizeObserver(fit).observe(host);\n  return ctx;\n}\n\nconst vcol = (n, f) => (getComputedStyle(document.body).getPropertyValue(n).trim()) || f;\n\nfunction grid(ctx, W, H, cols, rows){\n  ctx.strokeStyle = vcol(\"--line\", \"#222\");\n  ctx.lineWidth = 1;\n  ctx.beginPath();\n  for (let k = 1; k < cols; k++){\n    const x = Math.round(W * k / cols) + 0.5;\n    ctx.moveTo(x, 0); ctx.lineTo(x, H);\n  }\n  for (let k = 1; k < rows; k++){\n    const y = Math.round(H * k / rows) + 0.5;\n    ctx.moveTo(0, y); ctx.lineTo(W, y);\n  }\n  ctx.stroke();\n}\n\n/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *\n * Envelope display (reads params 0-3)\n * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */\nfunction makeADSRDisplay(host){\n  const ctx = dispCanvas(host);\n  const c = ctx.canvas;\n\n  function draw(){\n    const W = c._w, H = c._h, pad = 10;\n    ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);\n    grid(ctx, W, H, 8, 4);\n\n    const a = clamp(PV[0] != null ? PV[0] : 0.45, 0, 1);\n    const d = clamp(PV[1] != null ? PV[1] : 0.40, 0, 1);\n    const s = clamp(PV[2] != null ? PV[2] : 0.85, 0, 1);\n    const r = clamp(PV[3] != null ? PV[3] : 0.55, 0, 1);\n\n    const w = W - pad * 2, h = H - pad * 2;\n    const xA = pad + w * 0.26 * a;\n    const xD = xA + w * 0.26 * d;\n    const xS = xD + w * 0.16;\n    const xR = Math.min(W - pad, xS + w * 0.32 * r);\n\n    const pts = [[pad, H - pad], [xA, pad], [xD, H - pad - h * s], [xS, H - pad - h * s], [xR, H - pad]];\n\n    ctx.beginPath();\n    pts.forEach((p, k) => k ? ctx.lineTo(p[0], p[1]) : ctx.moveTo(p[0], p[1]));\n    ctx.strokeStyle = vcol(\"--accent\", \"#c8923a\");\n    ctx.lineWidth = 1.5;\n    ctx.stroke();\n\n    ctx.lineTo(xR, H - pad);\n    ctx.lineTo(pad, H - pad);\n    ctx.closePath();\n    ctx.globalAlpha = 0.10;\n    ctx.fillStyle = vcol(\"--accent\", \"#c8923a\");\n    ctx.fill();\n    ctx.globalAlpha = 1;\n\n    requestAnimationFrame(draw);\n  }\n\n  draw();\n}\n\n/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *\n * Ensemble display — three drifting lines, one per chorus tap\n * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */\nfunction makeEnsembleDisplay(host){\n  const ctx = dispCanvas(host);\n  const c = ctx.canvas;\n  const rd = host.querySelector(\".rd\");\n  let ph = 0;\n  let last = performance.now();\n\n  function draw(now){\n    const dt = Math.min(0.05, (now - last) / 1000);\n    last = now;\n\n    const rate = PV[8] != null ? PV[8] : 0.6;\n    const depth = PV[9] != null ? PV[9] : 0.65;\n    const mix = PV[10] != null ? PV[10] : 0.70;\n    ph += dt * rate;\n\n    const W = c._w, H = c._h;\n    ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);\n    grid(ctx, W, H, 6, 3);\n\n    for (let t = 0; t < 3; t++){\n      const off = t / 3;\n      const amp = H * 0.24 * (0.25 + depth * 0.75) * (0.55 + 0.45 * mix);\n      ctx.beginPath();\n      for (let x = 0; x <= W; x += 2){\n        const u = x / W;\n        const y = H / 2 + Math.sin((ph + off + u * 1.6) * Math.PI * 2) * amp\n                        + Math.sin((ph * 0.61 + off * 2 + u * 3.1) * Math.PI * 2) * amp * 0.35;\n        x ? ctx.lineTo(x, y) : ctx.moveTo(x, y);\n      }\n      ctx.strokeStyle = t === 0 ? vcol(\"--accent\", \"#c8923a\") : vcol(\"--accent-2\", \"#3fa98c\");\n      ctx.globalAlpha = t === 0 ? 1 : 0.55;\n      ctx.lineWidth = t === 0 ? 1.4 : 1;\n      ctx.stroke();\n    }\n    ctx.globalAlpha = 1;\n\n    if (rd) rd.textContent = Math.round(mix * 100) + \"% wet\";\n    requestAnimationFrame(draw);\n  }\n\n  requestAnimationFrame(draw);\n}\n\n/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *\n * Keyboard — on-screen keys AND the computer \"typing piano\",\n * both routed through the same press/release path.\n * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */\nconst KEYMAP = {\n  KeyA: 0, KeyW: 1, KeyS: 2, KeyE: 3, KeyD: 4, KeyF: 5, KeyT: 6,\n  KeyG: 7, KeyY: 8, KeyH: 9, KeyU: 10, KeyJ: 11, KeyK: 12, KeyO: 13,\n  KeyL: 14, KeyP: 15, Semicolon: 16\n};\n\nconst KEYLABEL = {\n  KeyA: \"A\", KeyW: \"W\", KeyS: \"S\", KeyE: \"E\", KeyD: \"D\", KeyF: \"F\", KeyT: \"T\",\n  KeyG: \"G\", KeyY: \"Y\", KeyH: \"H\", KeyU: \"U\", KeyJ: \"J\", KeyK: \"K\", KeyO: \"O\",\n  KeyL: \"L\", KeyP: \"P\", Semicolon: \";\"\n};\n\nconst NOTE_NAMES = [\"C\", \"C#\", \"D\", \"D#\", \"E\", \"F\", \"F#\", \"G\", \"G#\", \"A\", \"A#\", \"B\"];\n\nlet kbBase = 60;                 // note that KeyA plays\nconst held = new Map();          // note -> number of sources holding it\nlet keyElements = {};\n\nfunction keyEl(note){\n  return keyElements[note];\n}\n\nfunction pressNote(note){\n  const n = held.get(note) || 0;\n  held.set(note, n + 1);\n  if (n === 0){\n    noteOnHost(note, 100);\n    const el = keyEl(note);\n    if (el) el.classList.add(\"down\");\n  }\n}\n\nfunction releaseNote(note){\n  const n = held.get(note) || 0;\n  if (n <= 1){\n    held.delete(note);\n    noteOffHost(note);\n    const el = keyEl(note);\n    if (el) el.classList.remove(\"down\");\n  } else {\n    held.set(note, n - 1);\n  }\n}\n\nfunction releaseAll(){\n  Array.from(held.keys()).forEach(note => {\n    held.set(note, 1);\n    releaseNote(note);\n  });\n}\n\nfunction buildKeyboard(host){\n  const base = 48, octaves = 3;\n  const whitePattern = [0, 2, 4, 5, 7, 9, 11];\n  const blackPattern = { 1: 0, 3: 1, 6: 3, 8: 4, 10: 5 };\n  keyElements = {};\n\n  const whites = [];\n  for (let o = 0; o < octaves; o++){\n    for (const s of whitePattern) whites.push(base + o * 12 + s);\n  }\n\n  whites.forEach(n => {\n    const k = document.createElement(\"div\");\n    k.className = \"wk\";\n    k.dataset.note = n;\n    const lab = document.createElement(\"span\");\n    lab.className = \"kl\";\n    k.append(lab);\n    host.append(k);\n    keyElements[n] = k;\n  });\n\n  const wpc = 100 / whites.length;\n  for (let o = 0; o < octaves; o++){\n    for (const semi in blackPattern){\n      const n = base + o * 12 + (+semi);\n      const k = document.createElement(\"div\");\n      k.className = \"bk\";\n      k.dataset.note = n;\n      k.style.left = ((blackPattern[semi] + o * 7 + 1) * wpc - 2.5) + \"%\";\n      const lab = document.createElement(\"span\");\n      lab.className = \"kl\";\n      k.append(lab);\n      host.append(k);\n      keyElements[n] = k;\n    }\n  }\n\n  // ---- pointer input (multi-touch friendly) ----\n  const pointerNotes = new Map();\n\n  function noteFromEvent(e){\n    const el = document.elementFromPoint(e.clientX, e.clientY);\n    if (!el || !el.dataset) return null;\n    const target = el.dataset.note ? el : el.parentElement;\n    if (!target || !target.dataset || !target.dataset.note) return null;\n    return +target.dataset.note;\n  }\n\n  host.addEventListener(\"pointerdown\", e => {\n    const n = noteFromEvent(e);\n    if (n == null) return;\n    host.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId);\n    pointerNotes.set(e.pointerId, n);\n    pressNote(n);\n  });\n\n  host.addEventListener(\"pointermove\", e => {\n    if (!pointerNotes.has(e.pointerId)) return;\n    const n = noteFromEvent(e);\n    const cur = pointerNotes.get(e.pointerId);\n    if (n != null && n !== cur){\n      releaseNote(cur);\n      pointerNotes.set(e.pointerId, n);\n      pressNote(n);\n    }\n  });\n\n  function up(e){\n    const id = e.pointerId;\n    if (id != null && pointerNotes.has(id)){\n      releaseNote(pointerNotes.get(id));\n      pointerNotes.delete(id);\n      return;\n    }\n    // fallback channels (WKWebView can drop pointerup)\n    pointerNotes.forEach(n => releaseNote(n));\n    pointerNotes.clear();\n  }\n\n  host.addEventListener(\"pointerup\", up);\n  host.addEventListener(\"pointercancel\", up);\n  window.addEventListener(\"pointerup\", up, true);\n  window.addEventListener(\"mouseup\", up, true);\n  window.addEventListener(\"blur\", () => { pointerNotes.clear(); releaseAll(); });\n\n  relabelKeys();\n}\n\nfunction relabelKeys(){\n  document.querySelectorAll(\".piano .kl\").forEach(l => l.textContent = \"\");\n  for (const code in KEYMAP){\n    const note = kbBase + KEYMAP[code];\n    const el = keyEl(note);\n    if (el){\n      const lab = el.querySelector(\".kl\");\n      if (lab) lab.textContent = KEYLABEL[code];\n    }\n  }\n  const oct = Math.floor(kbBase / 12) - 1;\n  document.getElementById(\"octLabel\").textContent = NOTE_NAMES[kbBase % 12] + oct;\n}\n\nfunction typingPianoEnabled(){\n  const a = document.activeElement;\n  if (!a) return true;\n  if (a.isContentEditable) return false;\n  const tag = a.tagName;\n  return !(tag === \"INPUT\" || tag === \"TEXTAREA\" || tag === \"SELECT\");\n}\n\nconst downCodes = new Set();\n\nwindow.addEventListener(\"keydown\", e => {\n  if (e.metaKey || e.ctrlKey || e.altKey) return;\n  if (!typingPianoEnabled()) return;\n  const off = KEYMAP[e.code];\n  if (off == null) return;\n  e.preventDefault();       // the host would otherwise double-trigger the note\n  if (e.repeat || downCodes.has(e.code)) return;\n  downCodes.add(e.code);\n  pressNote(kbBase + off);\n});\n\nwindow.addEventListener(\"keyup\", e => {\n  const off = KEYMAP[e.code];\n  if (off == null) return;\n  e.preventDefault();\n  if (!downCodes.has(e.code)) return;\n  downCodes.delete(e.code);\n  releaseNote(kbBase + off);\n});\n\nwindow.addEventListener(\"blur\", () => {\n  downCodes.clear();\n  releaseAll();\n});\n\nfunction shiftOctave(dir){\n  downCodes.clear();\n  releaseAll();\n  kbBase = clamp(kbBase + dir * 12, 36, 84);\n  relabelKeys();\n}\n\n/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *\n * Boot\n * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */\nwhenReady(() => {\n  onParam((i, v) => { PV[i] = +v; });\n\n  document.querySelectorAll(\".knob-host\").forEach(makeKnob);\n  document.querySelectorAll(\".adsr\").forEach(makeADSRDisplay);\n  document.querySelectorAll(\".ens\").forEach(makeEnsembleDisplay);\n\n  buildKeyboard(document.getElementById(\"kbd\"));\n  document.getElementById(\"octDown\").onclick = () => shiftOctave(-1);\n  document.getElementById(\"octUp\").onclick = () => shiftOctave(1);\n});\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n","wasmBase64":"","explanation":"Orchestron 90 is an 8-voice string-machine synth: each voice stacks three detuned saws plus a sub square through a 2-pole SVF with envelope-tracked cutoff, then the mix runs into a three-tap ensemble chorus and a Schroeder plate reverb for that classic 90s string-pad wash. The flat stock-DAW-style GUI has hand-drawn knobs, a live envelope curve, an ensemble motion display, and a 3-octave piano playable by mouse/touch or the A…; typing-piano keys (with octave shift and preventDefault so the host doesn't double-trigger).","isInstrument":true,"locked":false,"provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-opus-5","effort":"medium","thinking":true,"promptHistory":["build me a 90s string synth"],"params":[{"name":"Attack","index":0,"min":0,"max":1,"default":0.45,"value":0.449999988079071},{"name":"Decay","index":1,"min":0,"max":1,"default":0.4,"value":0.400000005960464},{"name":"Sustain","index":2,"min":0,"max":1,"default":0.85,"value":0.850000023841858},{"name":"Release","index":3,"min":0,"max":1,"default":0.55,"value":0.550000011920929},{"name":"Cutoff (Hz)","index":4,"min":60,"max":14000,"default":3200,"value":635.7730102539062},{"name":"Resonance","index":5,"min":0,"max":1,"default":0.18,"value":0.309427082538605},{"name":"Env -> Cutoff","index":6,"min":0,"max":1,"default":0.35,"value":0.590345978736877},{"name":"Detune","index":7,"min":0,"max":1,"default":0.4,"value":0.200837060809135},{"name":"Ensemble Rate (Hz)","index":8,"min":0.05,"max":8,"default":0.6,"value":0.600000023841858},{"name":"Ensemble Depth","index":9,"min":0,"max":1,"default":0.65,"value":0.649999976158142},{"name":"Ensemble Mix","index":10,"min":0,"max":1,"default":0.7,"value":0.699999988079071},{"name":"Sub Level","index":11,"min":0,"max":1,"default":0.3,"value":0.300000011920929},{"name":"Reverb Mix","index":12,"min":0,"max":1,"default":0.35,"value":0.349999994039536},{"name":"Reverb Size","index":13,"min":0,"max":1,"default":0.6,"value":0.600000023841858},{"name":"Output Level","index":14,"min":0,"max":1,"default":0.7,"value":0.699999988079071}],"revisions":[{"id":1,"parent":0,"prompt":"build me a 90s string synth","assembly":"// ===========================================================================\n//  ORCHESTRON 90 — a 90s-style string ensemble synth\n//  8 voices, 3 detuned saws + sub square per voice, 2-pole SVF with envelope\n//  modulation, a 3-tap ensemble chorus and a Schroeder plate reverb.\n// ===========================================================================\n\nconst MAX_FRAMES: i32 = 8192;\nconst MAX_CHANNELS: i32 = 2;\nconst MAX_PARAMS: i32 = 64;\n\nconst NV: i32 = 8;              // polyphony\nconst CH_LEN: i32 = 4096;       // ensemble delay line\nconst CH_MASK: i32 = CH_LEN - 1;\nconst NLINES: i32 = 12;         // reverb delay lines\nconst REV_LEN: i32 = 14000;\n\nconst inBuf  = new StaticArray<f32>(MAX_FRAMES * MAX_CHANNELS);\nconst outBuf = new StaticArray<f32>(MAX_FRAMES * MAX_CHANNELS);\nconst params = new StaticArray<f32>(MAX_PARAMS);\n\nlet sampleRate: f32 = 44100;\nlet channels: i32 = 2;\n\n// ---- voice state ----------------------------------------------------------\nconst vP1 = new StaticArray<f32>(NV);\nconst vP2 = new StaticArray<f32>(NV);\nconst vP3 = new StaticArray<f32>(NV);\nconst vPS = new StaticArray<f32>(NV);   // sub phase\nconst vFreq = new StaticArray<f32>(NV);\nconst vVel = new StaticArray<f32>(NV);\nconst vEnv = new StaticArray<f32>(NV);\nconst vStage = new StaticArray<i32>(NV); // 0 idle 1 atk 2 dec 3 sus 4 rel\nconst vNote = new StaticArray<i32>(NV);\nconst vAge = new StaticArray<i32>(NV);\nconst vI1 = new StaticArray<f32>(NV);   // svf state\nconst vI2 = new StaticArray<f32>(NV);\nlet ageCounter: i32 = 1;\n\n// ---- ensemble chorus -----------------------------------------------------\nconst chBuf = new StaticArray<f32>(CH_LEN);\nlet chIdx: i32 = 0;\nlet lfoPh: f32 = 0;\n\n// ---- reverb --------------------------------------------------------------\nconst revBuf = new StaticArray<f32>(REV_LEN);\nconst lineOff = new StaticArray<i32>(NLINES);\nconst lineLen = new StaticArray<i32>(NLINES);\nconst lineIdx = new StaticArray<i32>(NLINES);\nconst combF = new StaticArray<f32>(NLINES);\n\nfunction clampf(x: f32, lo: f32, hi: f32): f32 {\n  if (x < lo) return lo;\n  if (x > hi) return hi;\n  return x;\n}\n\nexport function init(sr: f32, maxFrames: i32, ch: i32): void {\n  sampleRate = sr > 8000 ? sr : 44100;\n  channels = ch < MAX_CHANNELS ? ch : MAX_CHANNELS;\n\n  for (let v = 0; v < NV; v++) {\n    vP1[v] = f32(v) * 0.11;\n    vP2[v] = f32(v) * 0.27;\n    vP3[v] = f32(v) * 0.53;\n    vPS[v] = 0;\n    vFreq[v] = 220;\n    vVel[v] = 0;\n    vEnv[v] = 0;\n    vStage[v] = 0;\n    vNote[v] = -1;\n    vAge[v] = 0;\n    vI1[v] = 0;\n    vI2[v] = 0;\n  }\n\n  for (let i = 0; i < CH_LEN; i++) chBuf[i] = 0;\n  chIdx = 0;\n  lfoPh = 0;\n\n  // reverb line lengths (freeverb-ish), stereo spread of 23 samples\n  const baseLen = [1116, 1188, 1277, 1356, 556, 441];\n  let scale: f32 = sampleRate / 44100.0;\n  if (scale > 1.15) scale = 1.15;\n  if (scale < 0.5) scale = 0.5;\n  let off: i32 = 0;\n  for (let k = 0; k < NLINES; k++) {\n    const half: i32 = k < 6 ? k : k - 6;\n    let len: i32 = i32(f32(baseLen[half]) * scale) + (k < 6 ? 0 : 23);\n    if (len < 8) len = 8;\n    lineLen[k] = len;\n    lineOff[k] = off;\n    lineIdx[k] = 0;\n    combF[k] = 0;\n    off += len;\n  }\n  for (let i = 0; i < REV_LEN; i++) revBuf[i] = 0;\n\n  // defaults\n  params[0] = 0.45;    // attack\n  params[1] = 0.40;    // decay\n  params[2] = 0.85;    // sustain\n  params[3] = 0.55;    // release\n  params[4] = 3200.0;  // cutoff Hz\n  params[5] = 0.18;    // resonance\n  params[6] = 0.35;    // env -> cutoff\n  params[7] = 0.40;    // detune\n  params[8] = 0.60;    // ensemble rate Hz\n  params[9] = 0.65;    // ensemble depth\n  params[10] = 0.70;   // ensemble mix\n  params[11] = 0.30;   // sub level\n  params[12] = 0.35;   // reverb mix\n  params[13] = 0.60;   // reverb size\n  params[14] = 0.70;   // output level\n}\n\nexport function getInputPtr(): usize  { return changetype<usize>(inBuf); }\nexport function getOutputPtr(): usize { return changetype<usize>(outBuf); }\nexport function getParamsPtr(): usize { return changetype<usize>(params); }\nexport function getNumParams(): i32   { return 15; }\n\nexport function noteOn(id: i32, f: f32, v: f32): void {\n  // reuse a voice already holding this note, else a free one, else steal oldest\n  let slot: i32 = -1;\n  for (let i = 0; i < NV; i++) {\n    if (vNote[i] == id && vStage[i] != 0) { slot = i; break; }\n  }\n  if (slot < 0) {\n    for (let i = 0; i < NV; i++) {\n      if (vStage[i] == 0) { slot = i; break; }\n    }\n  }\n  if (slot < 0) {\n    let oldest: i32 = 0x7fffffff;\n    for (let i = 0; i < NV; i++) {\n      if (vAge[i] < oldest) { oldest = vAge[i]; slot = i; }\n    }\n  }\n  vNote[slot] = id;\n  vFreq[slot] = f > 8.0 ? f : 8.0;\n  vVel[slot] = clampf(v > 1.0 ? v / 127.0 : v, 0.05, 1.0);\n  vStage[slot] = 1;\n  vAge[slot] = ageCounter++;\n}\n\nexport function noteOff(id: i32): void {\n  for (let i = 0; i < NV; i++) {\n    if (vNote[i] == id && vStage[i] != 0 && vStage[i] != 4) vStage[i] = 4;\n  }\n}\n\nfunction combProc(k: i32, x: f32, fb: f32, damp: f32): f32 {\n  const off: i32 = lineOff[k];\n  const len: i32 = lineLen[k];\n  let idx: i32 = lineIdx[k];\n  const y: f32 = revBuf[off + idx];\n  let fl: f32 = combF[k];\n  fl = f32(y * (1.0 - damp) + fl * damp);\n  combF[k] = fl;\n  revBuf[off + idx] = f32(x + fl * fb);\n  idx++;\n  if (idx >= len) idx = 0;\n  lineIdx[k] = idx;\n  return y;\n}\n\nfunction apProc(k: i32, x: f32): f32 {\n  const off: i32 = lineOff[k];\n  const len: i32 = lineLen[k];\n  let idx: i32 = lineIdx[k];\n  const y: f32 = revBuf[off + idx];\n  revBuf[off + idx] = f32(x + y * 0.5);\n  idx++;\n  if (idx >= len) idx = 0;\n  lineIdx[k] = idx;\n  return f32(y - x);\n}\n\nfunction readCh(delaySamples: f32): f32 {\n  let pos: f32 = f32(chIdx) - delaySamples;\n  while (pos < 0) pos += f32(CH_LEN);\n  const i0: i32 = i32(pos) & CH_MASK;\n  const i1: i32 = (i0 + 1) & CH_MASK;\n  const frac: f32 = pos - Mathf.floor(pos);\n  const a: f32 = chBuf[i0];\n  const b: f32 = chBuf[i1];\n  return f32(a + (b - a) * frac);\n}\n\nfunction softClip(x: f32): f32 {\n  if (x > 1.6) return 1.0;\n  if (x < -1.6) return -1.0;\n  return f32(x - (x * x * x) * 0.14);\n}\n\nexport function process(n: i32): void {\n  const sr: f32 = sampleRate;\n\n  // --- envelope rates ---\n  const atkT: f32 = f32(0.004 + clampf(params[0], 0, 1) * clampf(params[0], 0, 1) * 3.0);\n  const decT: f32 = f32(0.03 + clampf(params[1], 0, 1) * clampf(params[1], 0, 1) * 3.0);\n  const sus: f32 = clampf(params[2], 0, 1);\n  const relT: f32 = f32(0.03 + clampf(params[3], 0, 1) * clampf(params[3], 0, 1) * 4.5);\n  const aInc: f32 = f32(1.0 / (atkT * sr));\n  const dInc: f32 = f32((1.0 - sus) / (decT * sr) + 0.0000001);\n  const rInc: f32 = f32(1.0 / (relT * sr));\n\n  // --- tone ---\n  const cutoff: f32 = clampf(params[4], 40.0, 16000.0);\n  const reso: f32 = clampf(params[5], 0, 1);\n  const envMod: f32 = clampf(params[6], 0, 1);\n  const detune: f32 = clampf(params[7], 0, 1) * 0.022;\n  const subAmt: f32 = clampf(params[11], 0, 1) * 0.7;\n  const kDamp: f32 = f32(2.0 - 1.85 * reso);\n\n  // --- ensemble ---\n  const rate: f32 = clampf(params[8], 0.02, 8.0);\n  const depth: f32 = clampf(params[9], 0, 1);\n  const ensMix: f32 = clampf(params[10], 0, 1);\n  const lfoInc: f32 = f32(rate / sr);\n  const baseD: f32 = f32(0.010 * sr);\n  const modD: f32 = f32(0.0055 * sr * depth);\n\n  // --- reverb ---\n  const revMix: f32 = clampf(params[12], 0, 1);\n  const size: f32 = clampf(params[13], 0, 1);\n  const fb: f32 = f32(0.70 + size * 0.27);\n  const damp: f32 = f32(0.18 + (1.0 - size) * 0.30);\n\n  const level: f32 = clampf(params[14], 0, 1);\n  const TWO_PI: f32 = 6.2831855;\n\n  for (let f = 0; f < n; f++) {\n    let mono: f32 = 0;\n\n    for (let v = 0; v < NV; v++) {\n      const stage: i32 = vStage[v];\n      if (stage == 0) continue;\n\n      // envelope\n      let e: f32 = vEnv[v];\n      if (stage == 1) {\n        e += aInc;\n        if (e >= 1.0) { e = 1.0; vStage[v] = 2; }\n      } else if (stage == 2) {\n        e -= dInc;\n        if (e <= sus) { e = sus; vStage[v] = 3; }\n      } else if (stage == 3) {\n        e = sus;\n        if (sus <= 0.0001) { e = 0; vStage[v] = 0; vNote[v] = -1; }\n      } else {\n        e -= rInc;\n        if (e <= 0.0) { e = 0; vStage[v] = 0; vNote[v] = -1; }\n      }\n      vEnv[v] = e;\n      if (vStage[v] == 0) continue;\n\n      // three detuned saws + sub square\n      const fr: f32 = vFreq[v];\n      const i1: f32 = f32(fr / sr);\n      const i2: f32 = f32(fr * (1.0 + detune) / sr);\n      const i3: f32 = f32(fr * (1.0 - detune * 0.85) / sr);\n      const iS: f32 = f32(fr * 0.5 / sr);\n\n      let p1: f32 = vP1[v] + i1; if (p1 >= 1.0) p1 -= 1.0;\n      let p2: f32 = vP2[v] + i2; if (p2 >= 1.0) p2 -= 1.0;\n      let p3: f32 = vP3[v] + i3; if (p3 >= 1.0) p3 -= 1.0;\n      let ps: f32 = vPS[v] + iS; if (ps >= 1.0) ps -= 1.0;\n      vP1[v] = p1; vP2[v] = p2; vP3[v] = p3; vPS[v] = ps;\n\n      let x: f32 = f32((p1 * 2.0 - 1.0) + (p2 * 2.0 - 1.0) + (p3 * 2.0 - 1.0)) * 0.30;\n      x += (ps < 0.5 ? f32(1.0) : f32(-1.0)) * subAmt * 0.30;\n\n      // 2-pole SVF, cutoff tracked by envelope\n      let fc: f32 = f32(cutoff * (1.0 + envMod * 5.0 * e));\n      const nyq: f32 = f32(sr * 0.45);\n      if (fc > nyq) fc = nyq;\n      if (fc < 30.0) fc = 30.0;\n      const g: f32 = Mathf.tan(f32(3.14159265 * fc / sr));\n      const a1: f32 = f32(1.0 / (1.0 + g * (g + kDamp)));\n      const a2: f32 = f32(g * a1);\n      const a3: f32 = f32(g * a2);\n      let ic1: f32 = vI1[v];\n      let ic2: f32 = vI2[v];\n      const v3: f32 = f32(x - ic2);\n      const vv1: f32 = f32(a1 * ic1 + a2 * v3);\n      const vv2: f32 = f32(ic2 + a2 * ic1 + a3 * v3);\n      ic1 = f32(2.0 * vv1 - ic1);\n      ic2 = f32(2.0 * vv2 - ic2);\n      vI1[v] = ic1;\n      vI2[v] = ic2;\n\n      mono += f32(vv2 * e * vVel[v]);\n    }\n\n    mono *= 0.42;\n\n    // ---- ensemble chorus (3 modulated taps, spread across the stereo field)\n    chBuf[chIdx] = mono;\n    lfoPh += lfoInc;\n    if (lfoPh >= 1.0) lfoPh -= 1.0;\n    const m1: f32 = Mathf.sin(f32(TWO_PI * lfoPh));\n    const m2: f32 = Mathf.sin(f32(TWO_PI * (lfoPh + 0.3333)));\n    const m3: f32 = Mathf.sin(f32(TWO_PI * (lfoPh + 0.6667)));\n    const t1: f32 = readCh(f32(baseD + modD * (1.0 + m1)));\n    const t2: f32 = readCh(f32(baseD * 1.35 + modD * (1.0 + m2)));\n    const t3: f32 = readCh(f32(baseD * 1.75 + modD * (1.0 + m3)));\n    chIdx = (chIdx + 1) & CH_MASK;\n\n    const wetL: f32 = f32(t1 * 0.62 + t3 * 0.38);\n    const wetR: f32 = f32(t2 * 0.62 + t3 * 0.38);\n    let dl: f32 = f32(mono * (1.0 - ensMix * 0.45) + wetL * ensMix);\n    let dr: f32 = f32(mono * (1.0 - ensMix * 0.45) + wetR * ensMix);\n\n    // ---- plate reverb ----\n    if (revMix > 0.001) {\n      const rin: f32 = f32((dl + dr) * 0.5 * 0.30);\n      let sL: f32 = 0;\n      sL += combProc(0, rin, fb, damp);\n      sL += combProc(1, rin, fb, damp);\n      sL += combProc(2, rin, fb, damp);\n      sL += combProc(3, rin, fb, damp);\n      sL *= 0.25;\n      sL = apProc(4, sL);\n      sL = apProc(5, sL);\n      let sR: f32 = 0;\n      sR += combProc(6, rin, fb, damp);\n      sR += combProc(7, rin, fb, damp);\n      sR += combProc(8, rin, fb, damp);\n      sR += combProc(9, rin, fb, damp);\n      sR *= 0.25;\n      sR = apProc(10, sR);\n      sR = apProc(11, sR);\n      dl = f32(dl * (1.0 - revMix * 0.5) + sL * revMix * 1.6);\n      dr = f32(dr * (1.0 - revMix * 0.5) + sR * revMix * 1.6);\n    }\n\n    const oL: f32 = softClip(f32(dl * level * 1.5));\n    const oR: f32 = softClip(f32(dr * level * 1.5));\n    outBuf[f] = oL;\n    outBuf[MAX_FRAMES + f] = oR;\n  }\n}\n","html":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\"/>\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"/>\n<title>Orchestron 90</title>\n<style>\n  :root{\n    --bg:#171717;\n    --panel:#1f1f1f;\n    --panel-2:#262626;\n    --track:#0d0d0d;\n    --line:rgba(255,255,255,.06);\n    --line-2:rgba(255,255,255,.11);\n    --line-3:rgba(255,255,255,.20);\n    --edge:rgba(255,255,255,.05);\n    --ink:#d7d7d9;\n    --ink-2:#9a9b9e;\n    --muted:#67696e;\n    --accent:#c8923a;\n    --accent-2:#3fa98c;\n    --radius:3px;\n    --radius-sm:2px;\n  }\n\n  *{box-sizing:border-box}\n  html,body{margin:0;height:100%}\n  body{\n    background:var(--bg);\n    color:var(--ink);\n    font:11px/1.4 ui-sans-serif,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,\"Segoe UI\",system-ui,sans-serif;\n    -webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;\n    -webkit-user-select:none;\n    user-select:none;\n    overflow-y:auto;\n  }\n\n  .app{display:flex;flex-direction:column;min-height:100%}\n\n  /* ---- top bar ---- */\n  .topbar{\n    display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:10px;\n    height:34px;padding:0 12px;\n    background:var(--panel);\n    border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);\n  }\n  .topbar .brand{font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink)}\n  .topbar .tagline{font-size:9px;letter-spacing:1.2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted)}\n  .topbar .sp{flex:1}\n  .topbar .hint{font-size:9px;letter-spacing:.6px;color:var(--muted)}\n  .topbar .hint b{color:var(--accent);font-weight:600}\n\n  .page{padding:10px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px}\n  .row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px;align-items:stretch}\n\n  /* ---- panels ---- */\n  .panel{\n    background:var(--panel);\n    border:1px solid var(--line);\n    border-top-color:var(--edge);\n    border-radius:var(--radius);\n    min-width:0;\n  }\n  .panel>.head{\n    display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;height:22px;padding:0 9px;\n    font-size:9px;letter-spacing:1.2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted);\n    border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);\n  }\n  .panel>.head .dot{width:5px;height:5px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--accent);opacity:.75}\n  .panel>.body{padding:10px;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start}\n\n  /* ---- control cell ---- */\n  .cell{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:4px;min-width:0}\n  .cell .lbl{font-size:9px;letter-spacing:.7px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-2);white-space:nowrap}\n  .num{\n    font-size:10px;color:var(--ink);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;\n    background:var(--track);border:1px solid var(--line-2);border-radius:var(--radius-sm);\n    padding:1px 6px;min-width:56px;text-align:center;\n  }\n\n  /* ---- knob ---- */\n  .knob{cursor:ns-resize;touch-action:none;display:block}\n  .knob .face{fill:var(--track);stroke:var(--line-2);stroke-width:1}\n  .knob .track{fill:none;stroke:var(--line-2);stroke-width:2.5}\n  .knob .arc{fill:none;stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:2.5;stroke-linecap:butt}\n  .knob .ind{stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:2;stroke-linecap:round}\n\n  /* ---- displays ---- */\n  .disp{position:relative;background:var(--track);border:1px solid var(--line-2);border-radius:var(--radius-sm)}\n  .disp canvas{display:block;width:100%;height:100%}\n  .disp .tag{position:absolute;top:4px;left:6px;font-size:8px;letter-spacing:.9px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted)}\n  .disp .rd{position:absolute;top:4px;right:6px;font-size:9px;color:var(--ink-2);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}\n\n  /* ---- buttons ---- */\n  .btn{\n    appearance:none;border:1px solid var(--line-2);border-top-color:var(--edge);\n    background:var(--panel-2);color:var(--ink-2);font:inherit;font-size:10px;font-weight:600;\n    letter-spacing:.4px;padding:4px 9px;border-radius:var(--radius-sm);cursor:pointer;min-width:30px;\n  }\n  .btn:hover{border-color:var(--line-3);color:var(--ink)}\n  .btn:active{background:var(--panel)}\n\n  /* ---- piano ---- */\n  .kbwrap{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;width:100%}\n  .kbbar{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px}\n  .kbbar .oct{font-size:9px;letter-spacing:.8px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-2);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}\n  .piano{\n    position:relative;height:80px;display:flex;\n    border:1px solid var(--line-2);border-radius:var(--radius-sm);\n    overflow:hidden;background:#000;touch-action:none;\n  }\n  .wk{\n    flex:1;background:#cbccce;border-right:1px solid #232323;cursor:pointer;\n    display:flex;align-items:flex-end;justify-content:center;padding-bottom:4px;\n  }\n  .wk.down{background:var(--accent)}\n  .bk{\n    position:absolute;top:0;width:5%;height:62%;background:#1c1c1e;z-index:2;cursor:pointer;\n    border:1px solid #000;border-top:0;border-radius:0 0 2px 2px;\n    display:flex;align-items:flex-end;justify-content:center;padding-bottom:3px;\n  }\n  .bk.down{background:var(--accent)}\n  .kl{font-size:8px;letter-spacing:.4px;color:#5a5b5e;pointer-events:none}\n  .bk .kl{color:#8c8d90}\n  .wk.down .kl,.bk.down .kl{color:#1a1206}\n\n  .tip{\n    position:fixed;z-index:50;background:#000;color:var(--ink);\n    border:1px solid var(--line-2);border-radius:var(--radius-sm);\n    padding:3px 7px;font-size:10px;pointer-events:none;white-space:nowrap;\n    opacity:0;transition:opacity .08s;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;\n  }\n  .tip.show{opacity:1}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"app\">\n\n  <div class=\"topbar\">\n    <span class=\"brand\">Orchestron 90</span>\n    <span class=\"tagline\">String Ensemble</span>\n    <span class=\"sp\"></span>\n    <span class=\"hint\">play with <b>A</b>&hairsp;…&hairsp;<b>;</b></span>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"page\">\n\n    <div class=\"row\">\n\n      <div class=\"panel\" style=\"flex:1 1 340px\">\n        <div class=\"head\"><span class=\"dot\"></span>Contour</div>\n        <div class=\"body\">\n          <div class=\"disp adsr\" style=\"flex:1 1 170px;height:118px;min-width:150px\">\n            <span class=\"tag\">Envelope</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"cell\">\n            <div class=\"knob-host\" data-index=\"0\" data-min=\"0\" data-max=\"1\" data-def=\"0.45\" data-disp=\"atk\"></div>\n            <div class=\"lbl\">Attack</div><div class=\"num\"></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"cell\">\n            <div class=\"knob-host\" data-index=\"1\" data-min=\"0\" data-max=\"1\" data-def=\"0.40\" data-disp=\"dec\"></div>\n            <div class=\"lbl\">Decay</div><div class=\"num\"></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"cell\">\n            <div class=\"knob-host\" data-index=\"2\" data-min=\"0\" data-max=\"1\" data-def=\"0.85\" data-disp=\"pct\"></div>\n            <div class=\"lbl\">Sustain</div><div class=\"num\"></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"cell\">\n            <div class=\"knob-host\" data-index=\"3\" data-min=\"0\" data-max=\"1\" data-def=\"0.55\" data-disp=\"rel\"></div>\n            <div class=\"lbl\">Release</div><div class=\"num\"></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"panel\" style=\"flex:1 1 300px\">\n        <div class=\"head\"><span class=\"dot\"></span>Tone</div>\n        <div class=\"body\">\n          <div class=\"cell\">\n            <div class=\"knob-host\" data-index=\"4\" data-min=\"60\" data-max=\"14000\" data-def=\"3200\" data-log=\"1\" data-disp=\"hz\"></div>\n            <div class=\"lbl\">Cutoff</div><div class=\"num\"></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"cell\">\n            <div class=\"knob-host\" data-index=\"5\" data-min=\"0\" data-max=\"1\" data-def=\"0.18\" data-disp=\"pct\"></div>\n            <div class=\"lbl\">Reso</div><div class=\"num\"></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"cell\">\n            <div class=\"knob-host\" data-index=\"6\" data-min=\"0\" data-max=\"1\" data-def=\"0.35\" data-disp=\"pct\"></div>\n            <div class=\"lbl\">Env&nbsp;Amt</div><div class=\"num\"></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"cell\">\n            <div class=\"knob-host\" data-index=\"7\" data-min=\"0\" data-max=\"1\" data-def=\"0.40\" data-disp=\"pct\"></div>\n            <div class=\"lbl\">Detune</div><div class=\"num\"></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"cell\">\n            <div class=\"knob-host\" data-index=\"11\" data-min=\"0\" data-max=\"1\" data-def=\"0.30\" data-disp=\"pct\"></div>\n            <div class=\"lbl\">Sub</div><div class=\"num\"></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"row\">\n\n      <div class=\"panel\" style=\"flex:1 1 340px\">\n        <div class=\"head\"><span class=\"dot\"></span>Ensemble</div>\n        <div class=\"body\">\n          <div class=\"disp ens\" style=\"flex:1 1 160px;height:96px;min-width:140px\">\n            <span class=\"tag\">Chorus</span><span class=\"rd\"></span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"cell\">\n            <div class=\"knob-host\" data-index=\"8\" data-min=\"0.05\" data-max=\"8\" data-def=\"0.60\" data-log=\"1\" data-disp=\"rate\"></div>\n            <div class=\"lbl\">Rate</div><div class=\"num\"></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"cell\">\n            <div class=\"knob-host\" data-index=\"9\" data-min=\"0\" data-max=\"1\" data-def=\"0.65\" data-disp=\"pct\"></div>\n            <div class=\"lbl\">Depth</div><div class=\"num\"></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"cell\">\n            <div class=\"knob-host\" data-index=\"10\" data-min=\"0\" data-max=\"1\" data-def=\"0.70\" data-disp=\"pct\"></div>\n            <div class=\"lbl\">Mix</div><div class=\"num\"></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"panel\" style=\"flex:1 1 230px\">\n        <div class=\"head\"><span class=\"dot\"></span>Space / Output</div>\n        <div class=\"body\">\n          <div class=\"cell\">\n            <div class=\"knob-host\" data-index=\"12\" data-min=\"0\" data-max=\"1\" data-def=\"0.35\" data-disp=\"pct\"></div>\n            <div class=\"lbl\">Reverb</div><div class=\"num\"></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"cell\">\n            <div class=\"knob-host\" data-index=\"13\" data-min=\"0\" data-max=\"1\" data-def=\"0.60\" data-disp=\"pct\"></div>\n            <div class=\"lbl\">Size</div><div class=\"num\"></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"cell\">\n            <div class=\"knob-host\" data-index=\"14\" data-min=\"0\" data-max=\"1\" data-def=\"0.70\" data-disp=\"pct\" data-size=\"62\"></div>\n            <div class=\"lbl\">Level</div><div class=\"num\"></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"panel\">\n      <div class=\"head\"><span class=\"dot\"></span>Keyboard</div>\n      <div class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"kbwrap\">\n          <div class=\"kbbar\">\n            <button class=\"btn\" id=\"octDown\">Oct &minus;</button>\n            <span class=\"oct\" id=\"octLabel\">C4</span>\n            <button class=\"btn\" id=\"octUp\">Oct +</button>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"piano\" id=\"kbd\"></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<script>\n\"use strict\";\n\n/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *\n * Engine bridge\n * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */\nfunction whenReady(cb){\n  function go(){ (window.vstai.onReady ? window.vstai.onReady(cb) : cb()); }\n  if (window.vstai) return go();\n  const t = setInterval(() => {\n    if (window.vstai) { clearInterval(t); go(); }\n  }, 25);\n}\n\nconst PV = {};   // last known value of every param, for the visualisers\n\nfunction setParam(i, v){\n  PV[i] = v;\n  if (window.vstai) window.vstai.setParam(i, v);\n}\n\nfunction onParam(cb){\n  if (window.vstai && window.vstai.onParam) window.vstai.onParam(cb);\n}\n\nfunction noteOnHost(n, v){\n  if (window.vstai && window.vstai.noteOn) window.vstai.noteOn(n, v);\n}\n\nfunction noteOffHost(n){\n  if (window.vstai && window.vstai.noteOff) window.vstai.noteOff(n);\n}\n\nconst clamp = (v, a, b) => Math.max(a, Math.min(b, v));\nconst ns = \"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\";\n\nfunction svgEl(t, a){\n  const e = document.createElementNS(ns, t);\n  for (const k in a) e.setAttribute(k, a[k]);\n  return e;\n}\n\n/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *\n * Tooltip\n * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */\nconst tip = document.createElement(\"div\");\ntip.className = \"tip\";\ndocument.body.append(tip);\n\nfunction showTip(text, x, y){\n  tip.textContent = text;\n  tip.style.left = (x + 12) + \"px\";\n  tip.style.top = (y + 14) + \"px\";\n  tip.classList.add(\"show\");\n}\n\nfunction hideTip(){\n  tip.classList.remove(\"show\");\n}\n\n/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *\n * Value formatting — mirrors the DSP's own param mappings\n * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */\nconst attackSec  = p => 0.004 + p * p * 3.0;\nconst decaySec   = p => 0.03 + p * p * 3.0;\nconst releaseSec = p => 0.03 + p * p * 4.5;\n\nfunction fmtTime(s){\n  return s < 1 ? Math.round(s * 1000) + \" ms\" : s.toFixed(2) + \" s\";\n}\n\nfunction formatValue(mode, v){\n  switch (mode){\n    case \"pct\":  return Math.round(v * 100) + \" %\";\n    case \"hz\":   return v >= 1000 ? (v / 1000).toFixed(2) + \" kHz\" : Math.round(v) + \" Hz\";\n    case \"rate\": return v.toFixed(2) + \" Hz\";\n    case \"atk\":  return fmtTime(attackSec(v));\n    case \"dec\":  return fmtTime(decaySec(v));\n    case \"rel\":  return fmtTime(releaseSec(v));\n    default:     return v.toFixed(2);\n  }\n}\n\n/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *\n * Knob — flat recessed disc, thin value arc, single indicator line\n * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */\nfunction makeKnob(host){\n  const i = +host.dataset.index;\n  const min = +host.dataset.min;\n  const max = +host.dataset.max;\n  const def = +host.dataset.def;\n  const log = host.dataset.log === \"1\";\n  const mode = host.dataset.disp || \"num\";\n  const size = host.dataset.size ? +host.dataset.size : 54;\n  const num = host.parentElement.querySelector(\".num\");\n\n  host.style.width = host.style.height = size + \"px\";\n\n  const svg = svgEl(\"svg\", { class: \"knob\", viewBox: \"0 0 100 100\", width: size, height: size });\n  const a0 = 135, a1 = 405, R = 38;\n\n  const polar = (deg, r) => [50 + r * Math.cos(deg * Math.PI / 180), 50 + r * Math.sin(deg * Math.PI / 180)];\n\n  function arcPath(from, to, r){\n    const [sx, sy] = polar(from, r);\n    const [ex, ey] = polar(to, r);\n    return \"M \" + sx + \" \" + sy + \" A \" + r + \" \" + r + \" 0 \" + (to - from > 180 ? 1 : 0) + \" 1 \" + ex + \" \" + ey;\n  }\n\n  svg.append(svgEl(\"circle\", { class: \"face\", cx: 50, cy: 50, r: R - 6 }));\n  svg.append(svgEl(\"path\", { class: \"track\", d: arcPath(a0, a1, R) }));\n  const arc = svgEl(\"path\", { class: \"arc\" });\n  const ind = svgEl(\"line\", { class: \"ind\" });\n  svg.append(arc, ind);\n  host.append(svg);\n\n  const toNorm = v => log ? Math.log(v / min) / Math.log(max / min) : (v - min) / (max - min);\n  const fromNorm = n => log ? min * Math.pow(max / min, n) : min + n * (max - min);\n\n  let value = def;\n\n  function render(){\n    const n = clamp(toNorm(value), 0, 1);\n    const ang = a0 + n * (a1 - a0);\n    arc.setAttribute(\"d\", arcPath(a0, Math.max(a0 + 0.001, ang), R));\n    const [ix, iy] = polar(ang, 13);\n    const [ox, oy] = polar(ang, R - 2);\n    ind.setAttribute(\"x1\", ix); ind.setAttribute(\"y1\", iy);\n    ind.setAttribute(\"x2\", ox); ind.setAttribute(\"y2\", oy);\n    if (num) num.textContent = formatValue(mode, value);\n  }\n\n  function set(v){\n    value = clamp(v, min, max);\n    render();\n    setParam(i, value);\n  }\n\n  let drag = null;\n\n  svg.addEventListener(\"pointerdown\", e => {\n    if (e.button !== 0) return;\n    drag = { y: e.clientY, n: clamp(toNorm(value), 0, 1) };\n    svg.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId);\n    showTip(formatValue(mode, value), e.clientX, e.clientY);\n  });\n\n  svg.addEventListener(\"pointermove\", e => {\n    if (!drag) return;\n    const speed = e.shiftKey ? 900 : 210;\n    set(fromNorm(clamp(drag.n + (drag.y - e.clientY) / speed, 0, 1)));\n    showTip(formatValue(mode, value), e.clientX, e.clientY);\n  });\n\n  function endDrag(){\n    if (drag){ drag = null; hideTip(); }\n  }\n\n  svg.addEventListener(\"pointerup\", endDrag);\n  svg.addEventListener(\"pointercancel\", endDrag);\n\n  svg.addEventListener(\"wheel\", e => {\n    e.preventDefault();\n    const step = e.shiftKey ? 0.005 : 0.025;\n    set(fromNorm(clamp(toNorm(value) - Math.sign(e.deltaY) * step, 0, 1)));\n  }, { passive: false });\n\n  svg.addEventListener(\"dblclick\", () => set(def));\n\n  onParam((p, v) => {\n    if (p === i){\n      value = clamp(+v, min, max);\n      PV[i] = value;\n      render();\n    }\n  });\n\n  set(def);\n}\n\n/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *\n * Canvas helpers\n * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */\nfunction dispCanvas(host){\n  const c = document.createElement(\"canvas\");\n  host.append(c);\n  const ctx = c.getContext(\"2d\");\n\n  function fit(){\n    const dpr = window.devicePixelRatio || 1;\n    c.width = Math.max(1, Math.round(host.clientWidth * dpr));\n    c.height = Math.max(1, Math.round(host.clientHeight * dpr));\n    ctx.setTransform(dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0);\n    c._w = host.clientWidth;\n    c._h = host.clientHeight;\n  }\n\n  fit();\n  new ResizeObserver(fit).observe(host);\n  return ctx;\n}\n\nconst vcol = (n, f) => (getComputedStyle(document.body).getPropertyValue(n).trim()) || f;\n\nfunction grid(ctx, W, H, cols, rows){\n  ctx.strokeStyle = vcol(\"--line\", \"#222\");\n  ctx.lineWidth = 1;\n  ctx.beginPath();\n  for (let k = 1; k < cols; k++){\n    const x = Math.round(W * k / cols) + 0.5;\n    ctx.moveTo(x, 0); ctx.lineTo(x, H);\n  }\n  for (let k = 1; k < rows; k++){\n    const y = Math.round(H * k / rows) + 0.5;\n    ctx.moveTo(0, y); ctx.lineTo(W, y);\n  }\n  ctx.stroke();\n}\n\n/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *\n * Envelope display (reads params 0-3)\n * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */\nfunction makeADSRDisplay(host){\n  const ctx = dispCanvas(host);\n  const c = ctx.canvas;\n\n  function draw(){\n    const W = c._w, H = c._h, pad = 10;\n    ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);\n    grid(ctx, W, H, 8, 4);\n\n    const a = clamp(PV[0] != null ? PV[0] : 0.45, 0, 1);\n    const d = clamp(PV[1] != null ? PV[1] : 0.40, 0, 1);\n    const s = clamp(PV[2] != null ? PV[2] : 0.85, 0, 1);\n    const r = clamp(PV[3] != null ? PV[3] : 0.55, 0, 1);\n\n    const w = W - pad * 2, h = H - pad * 2;\n    const xA = pad + w * 0.26 * a;\n    const xD = xA + w * 0.26 * d;\n    const xS = xD + w * 0.16;\n    const xR = Math.min(W - pad, xS + w * 0.32 * r);\n\n    const pts = [[pad, H - pad], [xA, pad], [xD, H - pad - h * s], [xS, H - pad - h * s], [xR, H - pad]];\n\n    ctx.beginPath();\n    pts.forEach((p, k) => k ? ctx.lineTo(p[0], p[1]) : ctx.moveTo(p[0], p[1]));\n    ctx.strokeStyle = vcol(\"--accent\", \"#c8923a\");\n    ctx.lineWidth = 1.5;\n    ctx.stroke();\n\n    ctx.lineTo(xR, H - pad);\n    ctx.lineTo(pad, H - pad);\n    ctx.closePath();\n    ctx.globalAlpha = 0.10;\n    ctx.fillStyle = vcol(\"--accent\", \"#c8923a\");\n    ctx.fill();\n    ctx.globalAlpha = 1;\n\n    requestAnimationFrame(draw);\n  }\n\n  draw();\n}\n\n/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *\n * Ensemble display — three drifting lines, one per chorus tap\n * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */\nfunction makeEnsembleDisplay(host){\n  const ctx = dispCanvas(host);\n  const c = ctx.canvas;\n  const rd = host.querySelector(\".rd\");\n  let ph = 0;\n  let last = performance.now();\n\n  function draw(now){\n    const dt = Math.min(0.05, (now - last) / 1000);\n    last = now;\n\n    const rate = PV[8] != null ? PV[8] : 0.6;\n    const depth = PV[9] != null ? PV[9] : 0.65;\n    const mix = PV[10] != null ? PV[10] : 0.70;\n    ph += dt * rate;\n\n    const W = c._w, H = c._h;\n    ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);\n    grid(ctx, W, H, 6, 3);\n\n    for (let t = 0; t < 3; t++){\n      const off = t / 3;\n      const amp = H * 0.24 * (0.25 + depth * 0.75) * (0.55 + 0.45 * mix);\n      ctx.beginPath();\n      for (let x = 0; x <= W; x += 2){\n        const u = x / W;\n        const y = H / 2 + Math.sin((ph + off + u * 1.6) * Math.PI * 2) * amp\n                        + Math.sin((ph * 0.61 + off * 2 + u * 3.1) * Math.PI * 2) * amp * 0.35;\n        x ? ctx.lineTo(x, y) : ctx.moveTo(x, y);\n      }\n      ctx.strokeStyle = t === 0 ? vcol(\"--accent\", \"#c8923a\") : vcol(\"--accent-2\", \"#3fa98c\");\n      ctx.globalAlpha = t === 0 ? 1 : 0.55;\n      ctx.lineWidth = t === 0 ? 1.4 : 1;\n      ctx.stroke();\n    }\n    ctx.globalAlpha = 1;\n\n    if (rd) rd.textContent = Math.round(mix * 100) + \"% wet\";\n    requestAnimationFrame(draw);\n  }\n\n  requestAnimationFrame(draw);\n}\n\n/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *\n * Keyboard — on-screen keys AND the computer \"typing piano\",\n * both routed through the same press/release path.\n * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */\nconst KEYMAP = {\n  KeyA: 0, KeyW: 1, KeyS: 2, KeyE: 3, KeyD: 4, KeyF: 5, KeyT: 6,\n  KeyG: 7, KeyY: 8, KeyH: 9, KeyU: 10, KeyJ: 11, KeyK: 12, KeyO: 13,\n  KeyL: 14, KeyP: 15, Semicolon: 16\n};\n\nconst KEYLABEL = {\n  KeyA: \"A\", KeyW: \"W\", KeyS: \"S\", KeyE: \"E\", KeyD: \"D\", KeyF: \"F\", KeyT: \"T\",\n  KeyG: \"G\", KeyY: \"Y\", KeyH: \"H\", KeyU: \"U\", KeyJ: \"J\", KeyK: \"K\", KeyO: \"O\",\n  KeyL: \"L\", KeyP: \"P\", Semicolon: \";\"\n};\n\nconst NOTE_NAMES = [\"C\", \"C#\", \"D\", \"D#\", \"E\", \"F\", \"F#\", \"G\", \"G#\", \"A\", \"A#\", \"B\"];\n\nlet kbBase = 60;                 // note that KeyA plays\nconst held = new Map();          // note -> number of sources holding it\nlet keyElements = {};\n\nfunction keyEl(note){\n  return keyElements[note];\n}\n\nfunction pressNote(note){\n  const n = held.get(note) || 0;\n  held.set(note, n + 1);\n  if (n === 0){\n    noteOnHost(note, 100);\n    const el = keyEl(note);\n    if (el) el.classList.add(\"down\");\n  }\n}\n\nfunction releaseNote(note){\n  const n = held.get(note) || 0;\n  if (n <= 1){\n    held.delete(note);\n    noteOffHost(note);\n    const el = keyEl(note);\n    if (el) el.classList.remove(\"down\");\n  } else {\n    held.set(note, n - 1);\n  }\n}\n\nfunction releaseAll(){\n  Array.from(held.keys()).forEach(note => {\n    held.set(note, 1);\n    releaseNote(note);\n  });\n}\n\nfunction buildKeyboard(host){\n  const base = 48, octaves = 3;\n  const whitePattern = [0, 2, 4, 5, 7, 9, 11];\n  const blackPattern = { 1: 0, 3: 1, 6: 3, 8: 4, 10: 5 };\n  keyElements = {};\n\n  const whites = [];\n  for (let o = 0; o < octaves; o++){\n    for (const s of whitePattern) whites.push(base + o * 12 + s);\n  }\n\n  whites.forEach(n => {\n    const k = document.createElement(\"div\");\n    k.className = \"wk\";\n    k.dataset.note = n;\n    const lab = document.createElement(\"span\");\n    lab.className = \"kl\";\n    k.append(lab);\n    host.append(k);\n    keyElements[n] = k;\n  });\n\n  const wpc = 100 / whites.length;\n  for (let o = 0; o < octaves; o++){\n    for (const semi in blackPattern){\n      const n = base + o * 12 + (+semi);\n      const k = document.createElement(\"div\");\n      k.className = \"bk\";\n      k.dataset.note = n;\n      k.style.left = ((blackPattern[semi] + o * 7 + 1) * wpc - 2.5) + \"%\";\n      const lab = document.createElement(\"span\");\n      lab.className = \"kl\";\n      k.append(lab);\n      host.append(k);\n      keyElements[n] = k;\n    }\n  }\n\n  // ---- pointer input (multi-touch friendly) ----\n  const pointerNotes = new Map();\n\n  function noteFromEvent(e){\n    const el = document.elementFromPoint(e.clientX, e.clientY);\n    if (!el || !el.dataset) return null;\n    const target = el.dataset.note ? el : el.parentElement;\n    if (!target || !target.dataset || !target.dataset.note) return null;\n    return +target.dataset.note;\n  }\n\n  host.addEventListener(\"pointerdown\", e => {\n    const n = noteFromEvent(e);\n    if (n == null) return;\n    host.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId);\n    pointerNotes.set(e.pointerId, n);\n    pressNote(n);\n  });\n\n  host.addEventListener(\"pointermove\", e => {\n    if (!pointerNotes.has(e.pointerId)) return;\n    const n = noteFromEvent(e);\n    const cur = pointerNotes.get(e.pointerId);\n    if (n != null && n !== cur){\n      releaseNote(cur);\n      pointerNotes.set(e.pointerId, n);\n      pressNote(n);\n    }\n  });\n\n  function up(e){\n    const id = e.pointerId;\n    if (id != null && pointerNotes.has(id)){\n      releaseNote(pointerNotes.get(id));\n      pointerNotes.delete(id);\n      return;\n    }\n    // fallback channels (WKWebView can drop pointerup)\n    pointerNotes.forEach(n => releaseNote(n));\n    pointerNotes.clear();\n  }\n\n  host.addEventListener(\"pointerup\", up);\n  host.addEventListener(\"pointercancel\", up);\n  window.addEventListener(\"pointerup\", up, true);\n  window.addEventListener(\"mouseup\", up, true);\n  window.addEventListener(\"blur\", () => { pointerNotes.clear(); releaseAll(); });\n\n  relabelKeys();\n}\n\nfunction relabelKeys(){\n  document.querySelectorAll(\".piano .kl\").forEach(l => l.textContent = \"\");\n  for (const code in KEYMAP){\n    const note = kbBase + KEYMAP[code];\n    const el = keyEl(note);\n    if (el){\n      const lab = el.querySelector(\".kl\");\n      if (lab) lab.textContent = KEYLABEL[code];\n    }\n  }\n  const oct = Math.floor(kbBase / 12) - 1;\n  document.getElementById(\"octLabel\").textContent = NOTE_NAMES[kbBase % 12] + oct;\n}\n\nfunction typingPianoEnabled(){\n  const a = document.activeElement;\n  if (!a) return true;\n  if (a.isContentEditable) return false;\n  const tag = a.tagName;\n  return !(tag === \"INPUT\" || tag === \"TEXTAREA\" || tag === \"SELECT\");\n}\n\nconst downCodes = new Set();\n\nwindow.addEventListener(\"keydown\", e => {\n  if (e.metaKey || e.ctrlKey || e.altKey) return;\n  if (!typingPianoEnabled()) return;\n  const off = KEYMAP[e.code];\n  if (off == null) return;\n  e.preventDefault();       // the host would otherwise double-trigger the note\n  if (e.repeat || downCodes.has(e.code)) return;\n  downCodes.add(e.code);\n  pressNote(kbBase + off);\n});\n\nwindow.addEventListener(\"keyup\", e => {\n  const off = KEYMAP[e.code];\n  if (off == null) return;\n  e.preventDefault();\n  if (!downCodes.has(e.code)) return;\n  downCodes.delete(e.code);\n  releaseNote(kbBase + off);\n});\n\nwindow.addEventListener(\"blur\", () => {\n  downCodes.clear();\n  releaseAll();\n});\n\nfunction shiftOctave(dir){\n  downCodes.clear();\n  releaseAll();\n  kbBase = clamp(kbBase + dir * 12, 36, 84);\n  relabelKeys();\n}\n\n/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *\n * Boot\n * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */\nwhenReady(() => {\n  onParam((i, v) => { PV[i] = +v; });\n\n  document.querySelectorAll(\".knob-host\").forEach(makeKnob);\n  document.querySelectorAll(\".adsr\").forEach(makeADSRDisplay);\n  document.querySelectorAll(\".ens\").forEach(makeEnsembleDisplay);\n\n  buildKeyboard(document.getElementById(\"kbd\"));\n  document.getElementById(\"octDown\").onclick = () => shiftOctave(-1);\n  document.getElementById(\"octUp\").onclick = () => shiftOctave(1);\n});\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n","explanation":"Orchestron 90 is an 8-voice string-machine synth: each voice stacks three detuned saws plus a sub square through a 2-pole SVF with envelope-tracked cutoff, then the mix runs into a three-tap ensemble chorus and a Schroeder plate reverb for that classic 90s string-pad wash. The flat stock-DAW-style GUI has hand-drawn knobs, a live envelope curve, an ensemble motion display, and a 3-octave piano playable by mouse/touch or the A…; typing-piano keys (with octave shift and preventDefault so the host doesn't double-trigger).","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-opus-5","wasmBase64":"","isInstrument":false,"timestamp":1787830736640,"params":[{"name":"Attack","index":0,"min":0,"max":1,"default":0.45,"value":0.45},{"name":"Decay","index":1,"min":0,"max":1,"default":0.4,"value":0.4},{"name":"Sustain","index":2,"min":0,"max":1,"default":0.85,"value":0.85},{"name":"Release","index":3,"min":0,"max":1,"default":0.55,"value":0.55},{"name":"Cutoff (Hz)","index":4,"min":60,"max":14000,"default":3200,"value":3200},{"name":"Resonance","index":5,"min":0,"max":1,"default":0.18,"value":0.18},{"name":"Env -> Cutoff","index":6,"min":0,"max":1,"default":0.35,"value":0.35},{"name":"Detune","index":7,"min":0,"max":1,"default":0.4,"value":0.4},{"name":"Ensemble Rate (Hz)","index":8,"min":0.05,"max":8,"default":0.6,"value":0.6},{"name":"Ensemble Depth","index":9,"min":0,"max":1,"default":0.65,"value":0.65},{"name":"Ensemble Mix","index":10,"min":0,"max":1,"default":0.7,"value":0.7},{"name":"Sub Level","index":11,"min":0,"max":1,"default":0.3,"value":0.3},{"name":"Reverb Mix","index":12,"min":0,"max":1,"default":0.35,"value":0.35},{"name":"Reverb Size","index":13,"min":0,"max":1,"default":0.6,"value":0.6},{"name":"Output Level","index":14,"min":0,"max":1,"default":0.7,"value":0.7}]}],"activeRevision":1,"nextRevisionId":2,"publishedAt":1787830824734}